cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the thesis below."
title: "Multi-Objective Resilient Urban Network Design & Disruption Management under Budget Constraints: A Reinforcement Learning Framework for the Case of Rivera, Uruguay"
authors:
  - family-names: "Spyropoulos"
    given-names: "Dimitrios"
    affiliation: "Department of Civil Engineering, University of Patras"
type: software
license: MIT
year: 2026
abstract: >-
  A three-stage reinforcement-learning framework for resilient urban transit network
  design. A tabular Q-learning agent restructures an existing network under hard
  coverage and budget constraints while deliberately leaving part of the budget
  unspent; 150 common-random-number Monte Carlo disruptions are then applied
  identically to every network; and a recovery agent spends the reserve to restore
  service without exceeding the approved budget. Case study: Rivera, Uruguay.
keywords:
  - transit network design
  - reinforcement learning
  - network resilience
  - disruption management
  - multi-objective optimisation
